\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The audit-stack control, on its own axes because it must not be read against Figure~\ref {fig:protocol}. Same protocol, same heads, same draws --- but a \emph  {rebuilt} detector stack, on which the separation \textbf  {inverts}: the memorized head scores 6/10 where the released head scores 0/10, the exact reverse of the deployment stack. This is why the behavioural certificate is joint in \emph  {(head, stack)} rather than a property of the head. An earlier draft drew this as an inset inside Figure~\ref {fig:protocol}, which invited precisely the cross-stack comparison the result forbids.}}{11}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
