\newlabel{tab:probectl}{{7}{11}{Positive control for the identity-blindness probe, 60 wrist frames at the home pose. $n$ counts frames in which \emph {both} chains detected. Rows below the floor are reported, never scored}{table.caption.27}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Substitution-probe attribution across heads: how far each head's predicted grasp point moves when one input is swapped between the two most-separated recorded episodes. The released head (v5) reads its \emph  {visual} channels (1.1--1.8\,cm) and barely moves on proprioception (0.09\,cm) --- the repair's signature. \textbf  {The counterexample that motivates pairing probes with behavioural randomization}: v2 and v2.1 have near-identical profiles on the jointly logged channels while scoring \textbf  {0.000 and 0.700} deployed. A probe evaluated on teacher trajectories is an on-manifold instrument and cannot, alone, certify off-manifold behaviour. (The two text blocks inside the plot area restate this caption and the v1 note; they are redundant with it and should be dropped when the figure is regenerated --- see the reproducibility note in \S  \ref {sec:limits}.) Hatched bars and $\times $ marks are channels not separately logged for that head, never zeros.}}{12}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:attribution}{{5}{12}{Substitution-probe attribution across heads: how far each head's predicted grasp point moves when one input is swapped between the two most-separated recorded episodes. The released head (v5) reads its \emph {visual} channels (1.1--1.8\,cm) and barely moves on proprioception (0.09\,cm) --- the repair's signature. \textbf {The counterexample that motivates pairing probes with behavioural randomization}: v2 and v2.1 have near-identical profiles on the jointly logged channels while scoring \textbf {0.000 and 0.700} deployed. A probe evaluated on teacher trajectories is an on-manifold instrument and cannot, alone, certify off-manifold behaviour. (The two text blocks inside the plot area restate this caption and the v1 note; they are redundant with it and should be dropped when the figure is regenerated --- see the reproducibility note in \S \ref {sec:limits}.) Hatched bars and $\times $ marks are channels not separately logged for that head, never zeros}{figure.caption.26}{}}
